{"contract":"translation_contextual_v2","candidate_identity":"28ce4bca4eba1772c970bdded09a9d95377f9014f1f6f591bdf3ec3ede7c18ab","verdicts":[{"revision_key":"54a6a1b06c2fb9c05197d9a9a5f9b3db865c80ef3946ed631f47277600d01022","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"54ef1fbfc9036ce7a6d07d438fc9a67b604d0c9d014893533d52934d64361d67","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"55bb0228d518ccd1fe3e72d745741a1a43c0cd53bb775ed0f5eacd7628b534c7","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"55dedd24042aae125f4b5dc8c45eb4688e9f1fc2d3283c3487fd82fc1a85cd5d","verdict":"ISSUE","observation":"The source text (demon.lua:151-157) refers to the player only through gendered placeholders (<?=player:he_she()?>/<?=player:him_her()?>). The translation twice replaces them with a hard-coded 「他」: 「阻止他冲破重围」 (source: before <?=player:he_she()?> can break through) and 「将他打成马蜂窝」 (source: reduce <?=player:him_her()?> to a flayed, quivering wreck). A female character therefore sees the wrong pronoun. Separately, 「familiarity」 in 「We have numbers, familiarity, tactics」 means familiarity with the power and combat, contrasting with the earlier line that the player does not know how to use the power properly. It is translated as 「团结精神」 (team spirit), which changes the meaning."},{"revision_key":"5666e9d8277742b7df95b3241b1eec6ab1fa1365323e2c65b7be28b88ed73126","verdict":"ISSUE","observation":"Several evaluative words are reversed or distorted (demon.lua:370): 「performing adequately in the less-direct ones」 means only adequate results, but it is translated as 「也有相当出色的表现」 (quite outstanding); 「the most straightforward of our competitions for the spectator」 means easiest for spectators to follow, but it is translated as 「最为熟悉」 (most familiar); 「with a sustainable amount of energy-input」 is translated as 「通过很少的能量」 (with very little energy). The source's contrast between 'devastating in the open field, only adequate in complex terrain' is lost."},{"revision_key":"59e30b6e11a96054bdfbe42947c9c14d018801b7a20c4e7e676479433f91a9d6","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"5b6924a79dbd71f8e223833298a0ed8058c2c7b7c10d0221ea66fb3effcb8204","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"5de8bdb19c931bdd1947728ce68ea9d0e79d5c3628a1841fcc3b86bc137e6cfb","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"5e4738cdc174e4c0df0456136df5a8567da5f2a9c567510bfbd4563f7376d408","verdict":"ISSUE","observation":"Several semantic errors (demon.lua:444ff): (1) 「only to lash out once I was sure my life was in danger」 means to strike back only once life is truly threatened, but it is translated as 「在真正有性命之虞的时候抽身逃走」 (slip away and flee), which reverses the meaning; (2) 「even the armies of Mal'Rok can't undo the effects」 is translated as 「哪怕乌鲁洛克的军队」, replacing the place name Mal'Rok with the demon god Urh'Rok (elsewhere in this entry Mal'Rok is 玛·洛克); (3) 「dripping acid into your eyes, then growing them back with more nerve endings than before」 means the eyes are regrown with more nerve endings, but it is translated as 「再将它放回神经更加密集的地方去」 (put it back somewhere with denser nerves); (4) 「an enraged horde of peasants」 is translated as 「大量的无知难民」 (refugees), but the source says peasants; (5) Cross-entry: Fearscape is 「恐惧空间」 here but 「恶魔空间」 in the same-batch entry 69b36890. This envelope has no frozen terminology evidence to decide which form is standard, but the batch is inconsistent."},{"revision_key":"614e1524636355ced3cb6890e9cee49a0e19efb8720e04b02185f20ab8057589","verdict":"ISSUE","observation":"Chat c in ashes-urhrok-walrog-pop.lua:62-65 is the player's reply 「The seas of Eyal shall know no lord」, and it is not limited by race. The only 'traitor' in the source is in chat b, where :tformat(kind == \"naga\" and \"Traitor\" or \"Murderer\") applies it to naga characters only. The translation adds 「无耻的背叛者？」 on its own, which is not in the source and is wrong for non-naga characters. Also, 「were their deaths just indecision?... I'll fix that」 mocks the player for being undecided about which side to take, and Walrog then offers to 'fix' that indecision. It is translated as 「那他们的尸体又是怎么回事？…还是让我来终结一切吧」, which loses the indecision meaning."},{"revision_key":"61c813b980b7ce4980e213759110affcbaec7b2368c9640838fdf96cda4efe19","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"61ee07b50ff6dcf70fbcc17e8a5718d4cc1975a7532768aa098153ccf3a7b227","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"620e36d2845505eccbc84482f63ade195ff3c2fcefd94c00b5eb1df1f9569eb7","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"633ee7605b9c379078bbd321cc06f2b56cad15f34ac77c1ba50ae6c8398d877d","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"641933080c0323cbfee34fceb1ef630eda1691351eb5abf98dfd325728e5c5c9","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"65e5cc822895bb51ab0ec61fe8cd5c1ecbff22e1b87d4da95c82b18bd0827dcf","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"676590b08fdf6a886055c04ba8bdc061408c6f69f15887dd1002cbd7f3d8a976","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"6815f464b006e6e9c9b68853c26bf99c450ca41035d3b0d9ab28e95e96182b1b","verdict":"OK"},{"revision_key":"69b36890678ee159bcf8d8af57235bfbe20b222a783193ef3d9c422ffb493080","verdict":"OK"}]}